# 3. Multiple matrices form an object

The program doesn't have just one matrix.

It has:

```python
matrices = [
    matrix1,
    matrix2,
    matrix3
]
```

For example:

```python
matrices = [

    [
        [1, 2, 3],
        [4, 5, 6]
    ],

    [
        [10, 20],
        [30, 40]
    ],

    [
        [100, 200, 300]
    ]

]
```

That means:

```text
Object
│
├── Matrix 1
│   ├── 1  2  3
│   └── 4  5  6
│
├── Matrix 2
│   ├── 10 20
│   └── 30 40
│
└── Matrix 3
    └── 100 200 300
```

The program can therefore tell you:

```text
Matrices: 3
```

